(5807709, 844365, 30982, '<td valign="top">Toning and depth of field for this are perfect.  First I see one little guy - cute puffed up little thing.  Then another.  Then another, and finally I realize there are at least four of them, yet each seems to be in its own little world.  A very pleasing photograph to visit.</td>', 'Toning and depth of field for this are perfect.  First I see one little guy - cute puffed up little thing.  Then another.  Then another, and finally I realize there are at least four of them, yet each seems to be in its own little world.  A very pleasing photograph to visit.', '2010-01-12 15:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5807712, 843988, 30982, '<td valign="top">You did this so nicely I thought the shoes WERE that way!  Maybe you need to go into both fashion design and fashion photograpy.  :-)  (But I''d miss your bird and wildlife shots if you did.)  PS - just noticed you finished next to another Sucker with diamond studded shoes. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-12 15:46:53.</i></td>', 'You did this so nicely I thought the shoes WERE that way!  Maybe you need to go into both fashion design and fashion photograpy.  :-)  (But I''d miss your bird and wildlife shots if you did.)  PS - just noticed you finished next to another Sucker with diamond studded shoes. ', '2010-01-12 15:46:10.000000', '2010-01-12 15:46:53.000000', 0),
(5807713, 844279, 30982, '<td valign="top">Amazing use of that focal plane/depth of field bit that I really need to pay more attention to.  The two birds are the perfect finishing touch to an awesome sky capture.</td>', 'Amazing use of that focal plane/depth of field bit that I really need to pay more attention to.  The two birds are the perfect finishing touch to an awesome sky capture.', '2010-01-12 15:48:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5807714, 844279, 30214, '<td valign="top">Robert, interesting how similar our photos are in subject matter and how close they ended up in scoring. You beat me by a fraction, though :). Great clouds!<br/> <br/>ETA: Deb and I are working in sync on the opposite sides of the globe :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-12 16:06:51.</i></td>', 'Robert, interesting how similar our photos are in subject matter and how close they ended up in scoring. You beat me by a fraction, though :). Great clouds! ETA: Deb and I are working in sync on the opposite sides of the globe :)', '2010-01-12 15:48:24.000000', '2010-01-12 16:06:51.000000', 0),
(5807716, 844265, 30982, '<td valign="top">Had I voted I might have recognized this as yours!  I like how you squeezed those cars all into that little space you created for them.</td>', 'Had I voted I might have recognized this as yours!  I like how you squeezed those cars all into that little space you created for them.', '2010-01-12 15:50:41.000000', NULL, 0),
